#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:44
msgid "64-bit, Prefetchable, GPU memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:45
msgid ""
"8 GB or 16 GB depending on GPU. Set to less than 2^44 to support P2P "
"access from other GPUs with a 44-bit physical address limit. Prefetchable"
" memory enables faster read operation for high-performance computing "
"(HPC) by fetching the contiguous data from the same data source even "
"before requested as an anticipation of a future request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:46
msgid "BAR2-3 registers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:47
msgid "64-bit, Prefetchable, Doorbell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:48
msgid ""
"Set to less than 2^44 to support P2P access from other GPUs with a 44-bit"
" physical address limit. As a Doorbell BAR, it indicates to the GPU that "
"a new operation is in its queue to be processed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:49
msgid "BAR4 register"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:50
msgid "Optional"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:51
msgid "Not a boot device"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:52
msgid "BAR5 register"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:53
msgid "32-bit, Non-prefetchable, MMIO"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:54
msgid "Is set to less than 4 GB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:57
msgid "Example of BAR usage on AMD GPUs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:58
msgid ""
"Following is an example configuration of BARs set by the system BIOS on "
"GFX8 GPUs with the 40-bit physical addressing limit:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:79
msgid "Details of the BARs configured in the example are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:81
msgid ""
"**GPU Frame Buffer BAR:** ``Memory at bf40000000 (64-bit, prefetchable) "
"[size=256M]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:83
msgid ""
"The size of the BAR in the example is 256 MB. Generally, it will be the "
"size of the GPU memory (typically 4 GB+). Depending upon the physical "
"address limit and generation of AMD GPUs, the BAR can be set below 2^40, "
"2^44, or 2^48."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:85
msgid ""
"**Doorbell BAR:** ``Memory at bf50000000 (64-bit, prefetchable) "
"[size=2M]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:87
msgid ""
"The size of the BAR should typically be less than 10 MB for this "
"generation of GPUs and has been set to 2 MB in the example. This BAR is "
"placed less than 2^40 to allow peer-to-peer access from other generations"
" of AMD GPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:89
msgid "**I/O BAR:** ``I/O ports at 3000 [size=256]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:91
msgid ""
"This is for legacy VGA and boot device support. Because the GPUs used are"
" not connected to a display (VGA devices), this is not a concern, even if"
" it isn't set up in the system BIOS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:93
msgid ""
"**MMIO BAR:** ``Memory at c7400000 (32-bit, non-prefetchable) "
"[size=256K]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:95
msgid ""
"The AMD Driver requires this to access the configuration registers. Since"
" the reminder of the BAR available is only 1 DWORD (32-bit), this is set "
"less than 4 GB. In the example, it is fixed at 256 KB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:97
msgid "**Expansion ROM:** ``Expansion ROM at c7440000 [disabled] [size=128K]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/Bar-Memory.rst:99
msgid ""
"This is required by the AMD Driver to access the GPU video-BIOS. In the "
"example, it is fixed at 128 KB."
msgstr ""

