#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/index.rst:9
msgid ""
"AI inference optimization is the process of improving the performance of "
"machine learning models and speeding up the inference process. It "
"includes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/index.rst:11
msgid ""
"**Quantization**: This involves reducing the precision of model weights "
"and activations while maintaining acceptable accuracy levels. Reduced "
"precision improves inference efficiency because lower precision data "
"requires less storage and better utilizes the hardware's computation "
"power."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/index.rst:13
msgid ""
"**Kernel optimization**: This technique involves optimizing computation "
"kernels to exploit the underlying hardware capabilities. For example, the"
" kernels can be optimized to use multiple GPU cores or utilize "
"specialized hardware like tensor cores to accelerate the computations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/index.rst:15
msgid ""
"**Libraries**: Libraries such as Flash Attention, xFormers, and PyTorch "
"TunableOp are used to accelerate deep learning models and improve the "
"performance of inference workloads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/index.rst:17
msgid ""
"**Hardware acceleration**: Hardware acceleration techniques, like GPUs "
"for AI inference, can significantly improve performance due to their "
"parallel processing capabilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/index.rst:19
msgid ""
"**Pruning**: This involves removing unnecessary connections, layers, or "
"weights from a pre-trained model while maintaining acceptable accuracy "
"levels, resulting in a smaller model that requires fewer computational "
"resources to run inference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/index.rst:21
msgid ""
"Utilizing these optimization techniques with the ROCm™ software platform "
"can significantly reduce inference time, improve performance, and reduce "
"the cost of your AI applications."
msgstr ""

