#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/model-acceleration-libraries.rst:14
msgid "Flash Attention 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/model-acceleration-libraries.rst:16
msgid ""
"Flash Attention is a technique designed to reduce memory movements "
"between GPU SRAM and high-bandwidth memory (HBM). By using a tiling "
"approach, Flash Attention 2 improves memory locality in the nested loops "
"of query, key, and value computations within the Attention modules of "
"LLMs. These modules include Multi-Head Attention (MHA), Group-Query "
"Attention (GQA), and Multi-Query Attention (MQA). This reduction in "
"memory movements significantly decreases the time-to-first-token (TTFT) "
"latency for large batch sizes and long prompt sequences, thereby "
"enhancing overall performance."
msgstr ""

