"to ``0``). Applies to MoE models with shared experts (for example, "
"DeepSeek-V3/R1 with 1 shared expert). Requires SiLU/GELU activation "
"(``is_act_and_mul``). Incompatible with `MoRI "
"<https://github.com/ROCm/mori#mori>`__ scheduling — disable with "
"``VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_FUSION_SHARED_EXPERTS=0`` if using MoRI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:120
msgid "``VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_FP4_ASM_GEMM``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:121
msgid ""
"Enable AITER assembly (HIP) FP4 GEMM kernels for MXFP4-quantized models "
"(defaults to ``0``). When set to ``1``, uses hand-tuned ASM kernels "
"instead of Triton for ``FP4×FP4`` weight GEMMs — faster at small batch "
"sizes (``M`` ≤ 64). Requires Instinct MI350X/MI355X (``supports_mx()``). "
"Combine with ``--quantization quark`` for MXFP4 models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:123
msgid "``VLLM_ROCM_USE_SKINNY_GEMM``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:124
msgid ""
"Prefer skinny-GEMM kernel variants for small batch sizes (defaults to "
"``1``). Improves performance when ``M`` dimension is small. **Recommended"
" to keep enabled**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:126
msgid "``VLLM_ROCM_FP8_PADDING``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:127
msgid ""
"Pad ``FP8`` linear weight tensors to improve memory locality (defaults to"
" ``1``). Minor memory overhead for better performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:129
msgid "``VLLM_ROCM_MOE_PADDING``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:130
msgid ""
"Pad MoE weight tensors for better memory access patterns (defaults to "
"``1``). Same memory/performance tradeoff as ``FP8`` padding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:132
msgid "``VLLM_ROCM_SHUFFLE_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:133
msgid ""
"This only affects the ``ROCM_AITER_FA`` backend. When set to ``0``, it "
"uses the HIP Paged Attention implementation "
"``torch.ops.aiter.paged_attention_v1`` from AITER. **Good for low "
"concurrency (for example, concurrency ≤32).** When set to ``1``, it uses "
"the ASM Paged Attention Kernel ``pa_fwd_asm`` from AITER. **Good for high"
" concurrency (for example, concurrency ≥32).** (Defaults to ``0`` when "
"AITER is on.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:135
msgid "``VLLM_ROCM_CUSTOM_PAGED_ATTN``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:136
msgid ""
"Use custom paged-attention decode kernel when ``ROCM_ATTN`` backend is "
"selected (defaults to ``1``). See :ref:`Attention backend selection with "
"AITER <vllm-optimization-aiter-backend-selection>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:144
msgid "Attention backend selection with AITER"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:146
msgid ""
"Most models work out of the box with ``VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1`` — vLLM "
"auto-selects the optimal backend. Use ``--attention-backend`` to override"
" the auto-selected backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:155
msgid ""
"Always set ``VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1`` even when using ``--attention-"
"backend`` explicitly. ``--attention-backend`` only overrides the "
"attention kernel; ``VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1`` is still required to enable "
"AITER for GEMM, RMSNorm, and MoE kernels. The Radeon/fallback backends "
"(``ROCM_ATTN``, ``TRITON_MLA``) are the exception — they do not use AITER"
" and do not require the env var."
msgstr ""

