#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:194
msgid "``--attention-backend ROCM_ATTN`` or ``TRITON_MLA``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:195
msgid ""
"``ROCM_ATTN`` is preferred over ``TRITON_ATTN`` — it uses a custom HIP "
"paged-attention kernel for decode when the model's KV head size is "
"supported, and falls back to Triton only when not. If ``ROCM_ATTN`` is "
"slow for your model (unsupported head size triggers Triton decode), try "
"``TRITON_ATTN``. Both work on Radeon GPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/vllm-optimization.rst:198
msgid ""
"**MoE models** (Mixtral, Llama-4-Scout/Maverick, DeepSeek-V2/V3/R1, "
"Kimi-K2.5, MiniMax-M2.5, GLM-5, Qwen-MoE): AITER MoE kernels activate "
"automatically with ``VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1`` — no extra attention backend"
" flags needed. If you hit ``RuntimeError: wrong! device_gemm ...``, set "
"``AITER_ONLINE_TUNE=1`` and retry. Only disable MoE kernels "
"(``VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_MOE=0``) if that also fails."
msgstr ""

