#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:10
msgid "AMD Instinct MI300 Series / MI350 Series workload optimization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:12
msgid ""
"This document provides guidelines for optimizing the performance of AMD "
"Instinct™ MI300X and MI350X GPUs, with a particular focus on GPU kernel "
"programming, high-performance computing (HPC), and deep learning "
"operations using PyTorch. It delves into specific workloads such as "
":ref:`model inference <mi300x-vllm-optimization>`, offering strategies to"
" enhance efficiency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:21
msgid ""
"Most guidance in this document applies to both MI300 Series (CDNA3, "
"gfx942, including MI300X and MI325X) and MI350 Series (CDNA4, gfx950, "
"including MI350X and MI355X). Where the two GPU families differ, GPU-"
"specific notes are provided. Key architectural differences include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:25
msgid ""
"**MI350 Series** uses TSMC N3P XCDs (vs N5), has 256 CUs (vs 304), 160 KB"
" LDS per CU (vs 64 KB), doubled Matrix Core throughput for ≤16-bit types,"
" native MXFP8/MXFP6/MXFP4 support, and 288 GB HBM3E at 8.0 TB/s."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:28
msgid ""
"**MI350 Series** uses 2 IODs (vs 4) with a faster direct connection, and "
"Infinity Fabric links run at 38.4 Gbps (vs 32 Gbps)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:30
msgid ""
"**MI350 Series** uses OCP FP8 variants (vs FNUZ on MI300 Series) and "
"moves TF32 from hardware to software emulation via BF16."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:36
