#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:309
msgid ""
"The following topics highlight :ref:`auto-tunable configurations <mi300x-"
"auto-tune>` as well as :ref:`Triton kernel optimization <mi300x-triton-"
"kernel-performance-optimization>` for meticulous tuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:314
msgid "Workload tuning strategy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:316
msgid ""
"By following a structured approach, you can systematically address "
"performance issues and enhance the efficiency of your workloads on AMD "
"Instinct MI300 Series and MI350 Series GPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:321
msgid "Measure the current workload"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:323
msgid ""
"Begin by evaluating the performance of your workload in its current "
"state. This involves running benchmarks and collecting performance data "
"to establish a baseline. Understanding how your workload behaves under "
"different conditions provides critical insights into where improvements "
"are needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:331
msgid "Identify tuning requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:333
msgid ""
"Analyze the collected performance data to identify areas where tuning is "
"required. This could involve detecting bottlenecks in CPU, GPU, memory, "
"or data transfer. Understanding these requirements will help direct your "
"optimization efforts more effectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:338
msgid ""
"Profiling is a fundamental step in workload tuning. It allows you to "
"gather detailed information about how your workload utilizes system "
"resources, and where potential inefficiencies lie. Profiling tools can "
"provide insights into both high-level and granular performance metrics. "
"See :ref:`mi300x-profiling-tools`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:344
msgid "High-level profiling tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:346
msgid ""
"For a broad overview, use tools like the :ref:`PyTorch Profiler <mi300x-"
"pytorch-profiler>`, which helps in understanding how PyTorch operations "
"are executed and where time is spent. This is particularly useful for "
"developers new to workload tuning, as it provides a comprehensive view "
"without requiring in-depth knowledge of lower-level operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:354
msgid "Kernel-level profiling tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:356
msgid ""
"When profiling indicates that GPUs are a performance bottleneck, delve "
"deeper into kernel-level profiling. Tools such as the :ref:`ROCr Debug "
"Agent <mi300x-rocr-debug-agent>`, :ref:`ROCProfiler <mi300x-rocprof>`, "
"and :ref:`ROCm Compute Profiler <mi300x-rocprof-compute>` offer detailed "
"insights into GPU kernel execution. These tools can help isolate "
"problematic GPU operations and provide data needed for targeted "
"optimizations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:365
msgid "Analyze and tune"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:367
msgid ""
"Based on the insights gained from profiling, focus your tuning efforts on"
" the identified bottlenecks. This might involve optimizing specific "
"kernel operations, adjusting memory access patterns, or modifying "
"computational algorithms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:372
msgid ""
"The following subsections discuss optimization ranging from high-level "
"and more automated strategies to more involved, hands-on optimization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:376
msgid "Optimize model inference with vLLM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:378
msgid ""
"vLLM provides tools and techniques specifically designed for efficient "
"model inference on AMD Instinct GPUs. See the official `vLLM installation"
" docs "
"<https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/getting_started/installation/gpu.html>`__"
" for installation guidance. Optimizing performance with vLLM involves "
"configuring tensor parallelism, leveraging advanced features, and "
"ensuring efficient execution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:385
msgid ""
"Configuration for vLLM: Set engine arguments according to workload "
"requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:388
msgid ""
"Benchmarking and performance metrics: Measure latency and throughput to "
"evaluate performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:393
msgid ""
"See :doc:`vllm-optimization` to learn more about vLLM performance "
"optimization techniques for MI300X, MI325X, MI350X, and MI355X."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:399
msgid "Auto-tunable configurations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:401
msgid ""
"Auto-tunable configurations can significantly streamline performance "
"optimization by automatically adjusting parameters based on workload "
"characteristics. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:405
msgid ""
"PyTorch: Utilize :ref:`PyTorch’s built-in auto-tuning features <mi300x-"
"torchinductor-tuning>`, such as the :ref:`TunableOp <mi300x-tunableop>` "
"module, which helps in optimizing operation performance by exploring "
"different configurations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:409
msgid ""
"MIOpen: Leverage :ref:`MIOpen’s auto-tuning capabilities <mi300x-miopen-"
"tuning>` for convolutional operations and other primitives to find "
"optimal settings for your specific hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:413
msgid ""
"Triton: Use :ref:`Triton’s auto-tuning features <mi300x-autotunable-"
"kernel-config>` to explore various kernel configurations and select the "
"best-performing ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:417
msgid "Manual tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:419
msgid ""
"Advanced developers can manually adjust parameters and configurations to "
"optimize performance. Both Triton and HIP involve manual tuning aspects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:422
msgid ""
"ROCm libraries: Optimize GPU performance by adjusting various parameters "
"and configurations within :ref:`ROCm libraries <mi300x-rocm-library-"
"tuning>`. This approach involves hands-on optimization to maximize "
"efficiency for specific workloads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:427
msgid ""
"Triton: Tune Triton kernels by adjusting parameters tailored to your "
"workload to :ref:`optimize GPU resource utilization <mi300x-triton-gpu-"
"utilization>` and better :ref:`leverage specific hardware features "
"<mi300x-assembly-analysis>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:432
msgid ""
"HIP: Profile and :ref:`optimize HIP kernels <mi300x-hip-optimization>` by"
" optimizing parallel execution, memory access patterns, and other "
"aspects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:436
msgid "Iterate and validate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:438
msgid ""
"Optimization is an iterative process. After applying tuning changes, re-"
"profile the workload to validate improvements and ensure that the changes"
" have had the desired effect. Continuous iteration helps refine the "
"performance gains and address any new bottlenecks that may emerge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:443
msgid ""
"ROCm provides a prebuilt optimized Docker image that has everything "
"required to implement the LLM inference tips in this section. It includes"
" ROCm, PyTorch, and vLLM. For more information, see :doc:`/how-to/rocm-"
"for-ai/inference/benchmark-docker/vllm`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:450
msgid "Profiling tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:452
msgid ""
"AMD profiling tools provide valuable insights into how efficiently your "
"application utilizes hardware and help diagnose potential bottlenecks "
"that contribute to poor performance. Developers targeting AMD GPUs have "
"multiple tools available depending on their specific profiling needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:457
msgid ""
"ROCProfiler tool collects kernel execution performance metrics. For more "
"information, see the :doc:`ROCProfiler <rocprofiler:index>` "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:462
msgid ""
"ROCm Compute Profiler builds upon ROCProfiler but provides more guided "
"analysis. For more information, see :doc:`ROCm Compute Profiler "
"documentation <rocprofiler-compute:index>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:466
msgid ""
"Refer to :doc:`profiling-and-debugging` to explore commonly used "
"profiling tools and their usage patterns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:469
msgid ""
"Once performance bottlenecks are identified, you can implement an "
"informed workload tuning strategy. If kernels are the bottleneck, "
"consider:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:472
msgid ":ref:`Auto-tuning in PyTorch with TunableOp <mi300x-tunableop>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:474
msgid ":ref:`Auto-tuning in MIOpen <mi300x-miopen-tuning>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:476
msgid ""
":ref:`Triton auto-tunable kernel configurations <mi300x-autotunable-"
"kernel-config>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:478
msgid ""
"If auto-tuning does not meet your requirements, consider :ref:`mi300x-"
"triton-kernel-performance-optimization`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:481
msgid ""
