msgid "Tensile optimization and performance tuning tips"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1210
msgid "MI16x16 versus MI32x32"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1211
msgid ""
"MI16x16 outperforms MI32x32 due to its superior power efficiency. The "
"MI16x16 format refers to the ``v_mfma`` instruction (such as "
"``v_mfma_f32_16x16x16f16``). See "
"`<https://llvm.org/docs/AMDGPU/AMDGPUAsmGFX940.html#vop3p>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1218
msgid ""
"MI350X has doubled Matrix Core throughput for ≤16-bit types. Benchmark to"
" verify optimal instruction size for your workload."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1221
msgid "Clock differences among XCDs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1222
#, python-format
msgid ""
"There can be a clock speed variation of 3% to 10% among different XCDs. "
"Typically, XCD0 has the highest clock speed, while XCD7 has the lowest on"
" MI300X. For optimal efficiency calculations on MI300X, use the XCD with "
"the lowest average clock speed. If the average clock speed of XCD0 is "
"used, target efficiencies (such as, 95% for DGEMM HPL cases with K=512) "
"may not be achievable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1229
msgid "`WorkGroupMapping`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1230
msgid ""
"To maximize L2 cache efficiency, use multiples of the XCD number. Both "
"MI300X and MI350X have 8 XCDs, so use multiples of 8 (such as, 24, 32, "
"40)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1233
msgid "GEMM stride issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1234
msgid ""
"On MI300, if the matrix stride in GEMM is a multiple of 512 bytes, it can"
" lead to Tagram channel hotspotting issues, causing a significant "
"performance drop, especially for TN transpose cases. This can increase "
"the latency of VMEM instructions and cause a notable performance drop. To"
" avoid this, use stride padding to ensure the stride is not a multiple of"
" 512 bytes (for instance, for TN F16 GEMM, set ``lda = ldb = K + 128`` "
"when ``K % 256 == 0``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1244
msgid "Optimizing Composable Kernel GEMM kernels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1246
msgid ""
"The performance of a GEMM kernel is significantly influenced by the input"
" values. The performance hierarchy based on input value types, from "
"highest to lowest, is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1250
msgid "Case 1: [all 0]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1252
msgid "Case 2: [all identical integers]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1254
msgid "Case 3: [random integers]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1256
msgid "Case 4: [random floats]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1258
msgid ""
"There can be more than a 20 percent performance drop between Case 1 and "
"Case 4, and a 10 percent drop between random integers and random floats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1261
msgid ""
"Additionally, ``bf16`` matrix core execution is noticeably faster than "
"``f16``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1263
msgid ""
"Distributing workgroups with data sharing on the same XCD can enhance "
"performance (reduce latency) and improve benchmarking stability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1269
msgid ""
"See :doc:`optimizing-with-composable-kernel` for an overview of "
"Composable Kernel GEMM kernels, information on tunable parameters, and "
"examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1276
msgid "MIOpen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1278
msgid ""
"MIOpen is AMD's open-source, deep learning primitives library for GPUs. "
"It implements fusion to optimize for memory bandwidth and GPU launch "
"overheads, providing an auto-tuning infrastructure to overcome the large "
"design space of problem configurations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1284
msgid "Convolution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1286
msgid ""
"Many of MIOpen kernels have parameters which affect their performance. "
"Setting these kernel parameters to optimal values for a given convolution"
" problem, allows reaching the best possible throughput. The optimal "
"values of these kernel parameters are saved in PerfDb (Performance "
"database). PerfDb is populated through tuning. To manipulate the tuning "
"level, use the environment variable ``MIOPEN_FIND_ENFORCE`` (1-6). "
"Optimal values of kernel parameters are used to benchmark all applicable "
"convolution kernels for the given convolution problem. These values "
"reside in the FindDb. To manipulate how to find the best performing "
"kernel for a given convolution problem, use the environment variable "
"``MIOPEN_FIND_MODE`` (1-5)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1301
msgid "Tuning in MIOpen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1303
msgid "``MIOPEN_FIND_ENFORCE=DB_UPDATE``, ``2``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1304
msgid "Performs auto-tuning and update to the PerfDb."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1306
msgid "``MIOPEN_FIND_ENFORCE=SEARCH``, ``3``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1307
msgid ""
"Only perform auto-tuning if PerfDb does not contain optimized value for a"
" given convolution problem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1310
msgid "What does :doc:`PerfDb <miopen:conceptual/perfdb>` look like?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1326
msgid "See :doc:`miopen:conceptual/perfdb` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1329
msgid "Finding the fastest kernel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1331
msgid "``MIOPEN_FIND_MODE=NORMAL``, ``1``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1332
msgid ""
"Benchmark all the solvers and return a list (front element is the fastest"
" kernel)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1334
msgid "``MIOPEN_FIND_MODE=FAST``, ``2``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1335
msgid ""
"Check FindDb (Find database) if convolution problem is found return - "
"else immediate fallback mode (predict the performing kernel parameters "
"based on mathematical and AI models)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1339
msgid "``MIOPEN_FIND_MODE=HYBRID``, ``3``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1340
msgid ""
"Check FindDb if convolution problem is found return - else benchmark that"
" problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1343
msgid "What does :doc:`FindDb <miopen:conceptual/finddb>` look like?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1361
msgid "See :doc:`miopen:how-to/find-and-immediate` for more information."
msgstr ""

