#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1871
msgid "Memory usage optimization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1860
msgid "Optimization for maximum throughput"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1862
msgid "Minimizing memory thrashing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1865
msgid "Parallel execution and GPU hardware utilization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1867
msgid ""
"The application should reveal and efficiently imply as much parallelism "
"as possible for optimal use to keep all system components active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1873
msgid ""
"To optimize memory throughput, minimize low-bandwidth data transfers, "
"particularly between the host and device. Maximize on-chip memory, "
"including shared memory and caches, to reduce data transfers between "
"global memory and the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1878
msgid ""
"In a GPU, global memory has high latency but a large size, while local "
"data share (LDS) has lower latency but a smaller size, and registers have"
" the fastest but smallest access. Aim to limit load/store operations in "
"global memory. If multiple threads in a block need the same data, "
"transfer it from global memory to LDS for efficient access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1886
msgid ""
"MI350X provides 160 KB LDS per CU (vs 64 KB on MI300X) with doubled read "
"bandwidth (256 bytes/clock) and direct L1→LDS loading, enabling "
"significantly more on-chip data reuse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1890
msgid ""
"See :doc:`HIP's performance guidelines <hip:how-"
"to/performance_guidelines>` for greater detail."
