#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1982
msgid "``rm -rf ~/.triton/cache``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1973
msgid "``python kernel.py | grep \"triton_gpu.shared = \" | tail -n 1``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1975
msgid ""
"You should see something like ``triton_gpu.shared = 65536``, indicating "
"65536 bytes of LDS are allocated for the kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1978
msgid ""
"Get number of waves per workgroup using the following steps (for example,"
" ``nW``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1984
msgid "``python kernel.py | grep \"triton_gpu.num-warps \" | tail -n 1``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1986
msgid ""
"You should see something like ``“triton_gpu.num-warps\" = 8``, indicating"
" 8 waves per workgroup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1989
msgid ""
"Compute occupancy limited by VGPR based on N according to the "
":ref:`preceding table <mi300x-occupancy-vgpr-table>`. For example, waves "
"per EU as ``occ_vgpr``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1993
msgid ""
"Compute occupancy limited by LDS based on L by: ``occ_lds = floor(65536 /"
" L)`` (MI300X, 64 KB LDS) or ``occ_lds = floor(163840 / L)`` (MI350X, 160"
" KB LDS)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1996
msgid ""
"Then the occupancy is ``occ = min(floor(occ_vgpr * 4 / nW), occ_lds) * nW"
" / 4``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:1998
msgid ""
"``occ_vgpr \\* 4`` gives the total number of waves on all 4 execution "
"units (SIMDs) per CU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:2001
msgid ""
"``floor(occ_vgpr * 4 / nW)`` gives the occupancy of workgroups per CU "
"regarding VGPR usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:2004
msgid "The true ``occ`` is the minimum of the two."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:2006
msgid ""
"Find the full ``occ.sh`` at `<https://github.com/ROCm/triton/blob/triton-"
"mlir/scripts/amd/occ.sh>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:2012
msgid "Gluon kernel performance optimization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:2014
msgid ""
"`Gluon <https://github.com/triton-"
"lang/triton/tree/main/python/triton/experimental/gluon>`_ is a block-"
"level programming language that ships alongside Triton. It compiles "
"through the same Triton IR stack and keeps Python ergonomics, but exposes"
" hardware details that Triton hides: explicit tensor **layouts**, "
"explicit async-copy and barrier placement, and direct control over LDS "
"usage. Use Gluon when the profiler shows Triton is bottlenecked on "
"something you cannot express through autotune configs — typically layout "
"conversions, suboptimal MFMA instruction selection, or pipelining depth."
msgstr ""

