#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:2060
msgid "Layout selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:2062
msgid ""
"Gluon requires you to pick layouts explicitly. The three that matter most"
" on MI300X / MI350X:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:2065
msgid "``AMDMFMALayout``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:2066
msgid ""
"Controls the output tile of MFMA instructions. Set ``transposed=True`` "
"for better accumulator register layout on CDNA. For a 256x256 tile with 4"
" waves, ``warps_per_cta=[2, 2]`` balances MFMA distribution across M and "
"N."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:2070
msgid "``PaddedSharedLayout``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:2071
msgid ""
"Preferred LDS layout for operand tiles. Padding eliminates bank conflicts"
" while preserving linear addressing and a single base VGPR. For a 256x64 "
"FP16 operand, ``PaddedSharedLayout([[512, 16]], ...)`` is a good starting"
" point. For FP8 with ``kWidth=32``, use dual-pass padding such as "
"``PaddedSharedLayout([[1024, 16], [2048, 32]], ...)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:2077
msgid "``DotOperandLayout`` (``kWidth``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:2078
msgid ""
"Controls how operand tiles feed MFMA. Use ``kWidth=8`` for FP16. For FP8 "
"without scales, use either ``kWidth=16`` or ``kWidth=32`` (both are "
"valid; both A and B operands must use the same value). For FP8 with "
"scales or MXFP4, use ``kWidth=16`` (required for scale-layout "
"compatibility)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:2083
msgid ""
"Avoid raw (unpadded, unswizzled) shared layouts. They trigger 2-way to "
"4-way LDS bank conflicts and reduce the effective LDS service rate from "
"256 B/cycle down to 64-128 B/cycle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:2088
msgid "MFMA instruction selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/inference-optimization/workload.rst:2090
msgid ""
"Match ``BLOCK_K`` to the MFMA K-dimension and aim for 1-2 MFMA "
"instructions per K-step to amortize pipelining overhead."
msgstr ""

