#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:487
msgid "Profiling with JAX XPlane Profiler"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:489
msgid ""
"MaxText has built-in XPlane profiling support via JAX's profiler. Traces "
"capture GPU kernel timelines, RCCL collectives, HLO graphs, and more. The"
" output can be viewed in TensorBoard's Trace Viewer or analyzed with "
"TraceLens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:495
msgid "Key MaxText profiler flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:497
msgid "The following MaxText config keys control profiling:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:506
msgid ""
"``steps`` should be greater than ``skip_first_n_steps_for_profiler`` + "
"``profiler_steps`` (for example, ``steps=12`` with ``skip=2`` and "
"``profile=5`` gives 5 warmup + 5 profiled + 2 cooldown). "
"``skip_first_n_steps_for_profiler=2`` skips step 0 (compilation) and step"
" 1 (warmup). ``profiler_steps=5`` is typically sufficient; more steps "
"produce larger ``.xplane.pb`` files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:514
msgid "Profiling with MAD or madengine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:516
msgid ""
"The model YAML configs under ``scripts/jax-maxtext/env_scripts/`` include"
" a ``profiler`` key (set to ``\"\"`` by default). To enable profiling "
"when running through MAD or madengine, edit the YAML config for your "
"model and set the profiler fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:529
msgid "Then run the benchmark as usual:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:540
msgid ""
"Use ``--keep-model-dir`` so the container's output directory is preserved"
" after the run. Profile output is written under the "
"``base_output_directory`` specified in the YAML."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:545
msgid "Example: Profile a model standalone in Docker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:590
msgid "Output structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:592
msgid "MaxText writes profiles in TensorBoard format:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:607
msgid "Viewing traces in TensorBoard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:616
msgid ""
"Navigate to **Profile > Trace Viewer** in the TensorBoard UI. Zoom into a"
" single training step (skip the first profiled step as it may have "
"residual warmup) and look at individual GPU streams to see compute/RCCL "
"overlap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:620
msgid ""
"To keep profile files small, use ``profiler_steps=5`` to keep "
"``.xplane.pb`` files under approximately 100 MB. Too many steps can "
"produce files over 500 MB that TensorBoard struggles to load. Use "
"``enable_checkpointing=False`` to avoid checkpoint I/O noise in the "
"trace, and ``dataset_type=synthetic`` to eliminate data loading "
"variability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../../../data/how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/previous-versions/jax-maxtext-v25.11-benchmark-models.yaml
#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:627
msgid "Profiling with rocprofv3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:629
msgid ""
"If you need to collect a trace without the JAX profiler, use "
"``rocprofv3``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/benchmark-docker/jax-maxtext.rst:636
msgid ""
"Replace ``<command>`` with the command you want to profile, such as "
"``./jax-maxtext_benchmark_report.sh -m Llama-2-7B``. Use ``-d "
