#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:7
msgid "Scaling model training"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:9
msgid ""
"To train a large-scale model like OpenAI GPT-2 or Meta Llama 2 70B, a "
"single GPU cannot store all the model parameters required for training. "
"This immense scale presents a fundamental challenge: no single GPU can "
"simultaneously store and process the entire model's parameters during "
"training. PyTorch provides an answer to this computational constraint "
"through its distributed training frameworks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:17
msgid "PyTorch distributed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:19
msgid ""
"Features in ``torch.distributed`` are categorized into three main "
"components:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:21
msgid ""
"`Distributed data-parallel training "
"<https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/generated/torch.nn.parallel.DistributedDataParallel.html>`_"
" (DDP)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:24
msgid ""
"`RPC-Based distributed training "
"<https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/rpc.html>`_ (RPC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:26
msgid ""
"`Collective communication "
"<https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/distributed.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:28
msgid ""
"In this topic, the focus is on the distributed data-parallelism strategy "
"as it’s the most popular. To get started with DDP, you need to first "
"understand how to coordinate the model and its training data across "
"multiple GPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:31
msgid "The DDP workflow on multiple GPUs is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:33
msgid ""
"Split the current global training batch into small local batches on each "
"GPU. For instance, if you have 8 GPUs and the global batch is set at 32 "
"samples, each of the 8 GPUs will have a local batch size of 4 samples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:36
msgid ""
"Copy the model to every device so each can process its local batches "
"independently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:38
msgid ""
"Run a forward pass, then a backward pass, and output the gradient of the "
"weights with respect to the loss of the model for that local batch. This "
"happens in parallel on multiple devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:41
msgid ""
"Synchronize the local gradients computed by each device and combine them "
"to update the model weights. The updated weights are then redistributed "
"to each device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:44
msgid ""
"In DDP training, each process or worker owns a replica of the model and "
"processes a batch of data, and then the reducer uses ``allreduce`` to sum"
" up gradients over different workers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:47
msgid ""
"See the following developer blogs for more in-depth explanations and "
"examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:49
msgid ""
"`Multi GPU training with DDP — PyTorch Tutorials "
"<https://docs.pytorch.org/tutorials/beginner/ddp_series_multigpu.html>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:51
msgid ""
"`Building a decoder transformer model on AMD GPUs — ROCm Blogs "
"<https://rocm.blogs.amd.com/artificial-intelligence/decoder-"
"transformer/README.html#distributed-training-on-multiple-gpus>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:57
msgid "PyTorch FSDP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:59
msgid ""
"As noted in :ref:`PyTorch distributed <rocm-for-ai-pytorch-distributed>`,"
" DDP model weights and optimizer states are evenly replicated across all "
"workers. Fully Sharded Data Parallel (FSDP) is a type of data parallelism"
" that shards model parameters, optimizer states, and gradients across DDP"
" ranks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:63
msgid ""
"When training with FSDP, the GPU memory footprint is smaller than when "
"training with DDP across all workers. This makes training some very large"
" models feasible by allowing larger models or batch sizes to fit on-"
"device. However, this comes with the cost of increased communication "
"volume. The communication overhead is reduced by internal optimizations "
"like overlapping communication and computation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:68
msgid ""
"For a high-level overview of how FSDP works, review `Getting started with"
" Fully Sharded Data Parallel "
"<https://pytorch.org/tutorials/intermediate/FSDP_tutorial.html#how-fsdp-"
"works>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:71
msgid ""
"For detailed training steps, see `PyTorch FSDP examples "
"<https://github.com/pytorch/examples/tree/main/distributed/FSDP>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:77
msgid "DeepSpeed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:79
msgid ""
"`DeepSpeed <https://deepspeed.ai>`_ offers system innovations that make "
"large-scale deep learning training effective, efficient, and easy to use."
" Innovations such as ZeRO, 3D-Parallelism, DeepSpeed-MoE, ZeRO-Infinity, "
"and so on fall under the training pillar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:83
msgid ""
"See `Pre-training a large language model with Megatron-DeepSpeed on "
"multiple AMD GPUs <https://rocm.blogs.amd.com/artificial-intelligence"
"/megatron-deepspeed-pretrain/README.html>`_ for a detailed example of "
"training with DeepSpeed on an AMD GPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:90
msgid "Automatic mixed precision (AMP)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:92
msgid ""
"As models increase in size, so do the time and memory needed to train "
"them; their cost also increases. Any measure we can take to reduce "
"training time and memory usage through `automatic mixed precision "
"<https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/amp.html>`_ (AMP) is highly beneficial "
"for most use cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/rocm-for-ai/training/scale-model-training.rst:96
msgid ""
"See `Automatic mixed precision in PyTorch using AMD GPUs — ROCm Blogs "
"<https://rocm.blogs.amd.com/artificial-intelligence/automatic-mixed-"
"precision/README.html#automatic-mixed-precision-in-pytorch-using-amd-"
"gpus>`_ for more information about running AMP on an AMD Instinct-Series "
"GPU."
msgstr ""

