#: ../../how-to/setting-cus.rst:9
msgid "Setting the number of compute units"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/setting-cus.rst:11
msgid ""
"The GPU driver provides two environment variables to set the number of "
"CUs used:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/setting-cus.rst:13
msgid "``HSA_CU_MASK``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/setting-cus.rst:14
msgid "``ROC_GLOBAL_CU_MASK``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/setting-cus.rst:16
msgid ""
"The ``ROC_GLOBAL_CU_MASK`` variable sets the CU mask on queues created by"
" HIP or OpenCL runtimes. The ``HSA_CU_MASK`` variable sets the mask on a "
"lower level of queue creation in the driver. It also sets the mask on the"
" queues being profiled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/setting-cus.rst:20
msgid ""
"When using GPUs to accelerate compute workloads, it sometimes becomes "
"necessary to configure the hardware's usage of compute units (CU). This "
"is a more advanced option, so please read this page before "
"experimentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/setting-cus.rst:22
msgid "The environment variables have the following syntax:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/setting-cus.rst:33
msgid ""
"The GPU indices are taken post ``ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES`` reordering. The "
"listed or masked CUs are enabled for listed GPUs, and the others are "
"disabled. Unlisted GPUs are not be affected, and their CUs are enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/setting-cus.rst:35
msgid ""
"The variable parsing stops when a syntax error occurs. The erroneous set "
"and the following are ignored. Repeating GPU or CU IDs results in a "
"syntax error. Specifying a mask with no usable CUs (CU_list is 0x0) "
"results in a syntax error. To exclude GPU devices, use "
"``ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/setting-cus.rst:39
msgid ""
"These environment variables only affect ROCm software, not graphics "
"applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/setting-cus.rst:41
msgid ""
"Not all CU configurations are valid on all devices. For example, on "
"devices where two CUs can be combined into a WGP (for kernels running in "
"WGP mode), it’s not valid to disable only a single CU in a WGP."
msgstr ""

